/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Framing is the one thing a consent screen must never allow, so it is covered
# twice (frame-ancestors + X-Frame-Options). object-src/base-uri/form-action are
# safe to pin here: the app embeds no plugins, needs no <base>, and only ever
# submits forms to its own origin (the consent decision goes to the issuer over
# fetch, not a form POST), so these cost nothing and shrink the injection surface.
#
# No script-src/connect-src yet: the app fetches the OSN issuer, whose origin
# differs per environment, and a wrong connect-src breaks sign-in outright. Those
# two need a build-time policy generated from VITE_OSN_ISSUER_URL against the
# emitted bundle — tracked as S-L3 in wiki/TODO.md.
